  "recipeCuisine": "France",
  "name": "Hollandaise Sauce",
  "text": "Hollandaise Sauce\n\nPreparation Time: 20 minutes\n\nCooking time: 12-15 minutes\n\nYield: 2-3\n\nIngredients\n\n2 tbsp cold water,\n\n½ tbsp white wine vinegar,\n\n½ tsp white peppercorns (crushed),\n\n2 egg yolks,\n\n125g unsalted butter (freshly clarified, and cooled to tepid),\n\nJuice of ¼ lemon.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Combine the water, vinegar and pepper into a small saucepan.\n\n2. Over a low heat reduce by one third then leave to cool.\n\n3. Put the egg yolks into a glass bowl and add the cold liquid.\n\n4. Mix thoroughly with a small whisk.\n\n5. Set the boil over a pan of gently boiling water and whisk continually until the mixture becomes smooth and creamy after 8-10 minutes.\n\n6. Take the bowl off the heat.\n\n7. Gradually add the cooled clarified butter, initially a drop at a time, gradually increasing.",
  "prepTime": "PT20M",
  "recipeYield": "2-3",
